     "varsMobile": {},
     "css": "[data-block=\"417d7d39d9e6446b0f76\"] { mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-accordion-block-blend\n); border-radius: var(--tweak-accordion-block-radius); }",
     "type": "accordion",
     "items": [
      {
       "title": "How important is attendance & communication?",
       "html": "<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Consistent attendance helps participants become familiar with their routine, instructors, and peers. Families should notify EduBud as early as possible regarding absences, late arrivals, early pickups, transportation changes, or other schedule changes. Please keep emergency contacts and important participant information up to date.</p>"
      },
      {
       "title": "What does it take to qualify for Edubud?",
       "html": "<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">A diagnosis alone does not determine whether someone is a good fit for EduBud. We look at the whole person, their strengths, interests, communication style, independence, support needs, and ability to safely participate in our community.&#160; Our goal is to create an environment where participants can belong, learn, grow, and be themselves.</p>"
      },
      {
       "title": "What are other programs offered outside of the community center?",
       "html": "<p style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Edubud offers Buddy Program Projects that connect our participants with well-trained Buddy Partners who are highly skilled and prepared to work with individuals in the special needs community. Buddies provide encouragement, companionship, and support during activities, community outings, and other special social experiences. Volunteers may also participate in special events, community service projects, and other meaningful opportunities that promote friendship, independence, and inclusion. If you are interested, more information is available on our “golden bridge” tab.</p>"
      }
     ],
